// when there is none. procs is an array of P*; entry `tag` is itself a P*.
//
// Two ways to have none, and 0 is the right answer to both: the tag names no P at all
// (MSPAN_OWNING_P_RAW / _PARKED), or the scheduler has not published __sched_procs yet. Returning 0
// rather than throwing is deliberate — "there is no P" is the NORMAL answer on a raw OS thread and
// on every program that never starts a scheduler, and every caller already handles it.
//
// ⚠ The tag gate also closes a wild deref the old `id < 0` gate did not: it caught -1 but NOT the
// 0xFFFFFFFF parked sentinel, which a raw-thread free of a parked span would have used to index
// `__sched_procs` four billion entries out. It now routes to the same fallback-local push a missing
