// Is a multi-P scheduler up? P[0] is published before any worker exists, so a non-null entry there
// is the one observable that says "another thread may now be allocating". Named because two call
// sites ask it (`__slab_alloc_needzero`, `__slab_free`) and `__slab_proc_at(0) != 0` states the
// mechanism rather than the question.
function __slab_scheduler_is_running() returns bool
