// Return the physical backing of GENUINELY IDLE fully-free spans parked in mcentral
// to the OS, dropping the resident set without giving up the arena's address space.
// Every span on a class's partial list is fully free by construction
// (__slab_mcentral_return_span only ever prepends fully-emptied spans, and
// __slab_refill_mcache removes a span before handing it to a P).
//
// A two-epoch grace guard (the +0x48 state) gates the actual decommit: a span is
// only handed back once it has been observed fully free by TWO consecutive scavenge
// passes without an intervening reuse. This keeps the active working set — spans
// freed and reused between passes — committed, avoiding decommit/recommit thrash.
//
// Runs entirely under the global __slab_lock so it cannot race an allocation that
// pulls a span off the same partial list.
function __slab_scavenge()
