// Buffer-level Copy-On-Write. If capacity >= 0 AND the record is not INLINE the
// buffer is already mm_alloc-owned, writable, and independently reallocatable —
// no-op. Otherwise (capacity < 0: rdata = -2 or slice = -1; OR parent == INLINE:
// buffer lives inside the record's own slab slot and cannot be `mmRealloc`'d)
// the buffer is shared / read-only / non-detachable; allocate a fresh
// length*elemSize-byte EXTERNAL buffer, memcpy the live bytes out, and rewire
// self.buffer + self.capacity so the record becomes an ordinary ROOT array. The
// old rdata/slice/inline buffer is intentionally NOT freed (rdata is in the
// binary's read-only section; slice buffers are owned by their parent; inline
// bytes are reclaimed when the record's own slot is freed). Non-throwing.
function __managed_mem_cow_check(self MachineWord) returns MachineWord
