	// `__destruct___ManagedMemory` keys teardown on parent_ptr (NOT capacity), so
	// without this the record kept its pre-COW parent — RDATA (-2: "nothing to
	// free", so the new owned buffer leaked — the append/grow-from-literal leak),
	// INLINE (-3: a non-pointer marker, never a heap ref to decref), or a slice
	// parent (whose ref we must now drop, since we no longer alias its buffer). Set
	// ROOT, then release ONLY a real slice parent (a heap pointer, i.e. not one of
	// the ROOT/INLINE/RDATA/UNINIT sentinels). `parent` was read at entry.
	__Internals.storeIndirect(self + MM_OFFSET_PARENT, value: MM_PARENT_ROOT)
