	// zero-copy view is a slice (capacity -1, shared with its parent): the in-place
	// tail-shift below would fault on rdata or corrupt the parent on a slice.
	// Materialize a private, writable heap buffer first — mirroring `set`/`swap`
	// (same `capacity < 0` gate) and the C# reference `LowerManagedMemRemove`, which
	// emits an `EmitCowCheck` before the shift. An owned ROOT/INLINE buffer
	// (capacity >= 0) is already writable, so cow_check is skipped.
